e order. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array is indexed by edge position. A view is a snapshot, so its own positions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only until its next mutation: the view of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"text":", inserting","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one cell shifts every later incidence by one).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every index member reads the base’s rows, shifted where they hold hyperedges:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successorIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"text":" plus n, and of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"text":" it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"targetIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"predecessorIndices"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inHyperedgeIndices"},{"text":" plus n, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sourceIndices"},{"text":". Graph algorithms therefore run on the view without hashing a vertex. The view","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"does not offer ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withSuccessorIndexRows"},{"text":", whose contract needs edge positions in row order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Costs are as for "},{"code":"IncidenceGraphView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": O(1) reads on "},{"code":"IncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which stores its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidences; on another base a hyperedge’s incidence numbers are a range, O(1), "},{"code":"edges[q]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binary-searches and selects by rank, O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on "},{"code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"code":"outEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"inEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is computed from "},{"code":"_memberRank","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n + m"},{"type":"text","text":" whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i < n"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" and whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" is hyperedge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", with an arc "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i → n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" for each source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p → j"},{"type":"text","text":" for each target "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"j"},{"type":"text","text":". A vertex on both sides of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the 2